    ('Neon arrow pointing downward', 'Look for a simple but striking downward-pointing arrow made of neon tubes, typically directing people to a basement bar, restaurant, or business entrance below street level.', 'Identify neon tubing shaped as an arrow with the point directed downward. The arrow must be clearly visible in glowing neon with an unmistakable downward direction.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Downward-pointing neon arrows were primarily used to direct pedestrians to basement-level establishments during the 1940s-50s urban expansion boom.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/b7267ac993233221.jpg', 4),
